{"id":"NCT07142356","title":"A Study of Modified Release RTN-001 In Patients With Uncontrolled Hypertension","official":"A Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo Controlled, Parallel Group, Multicenter Study of Modified Release RTN-001 In Patients With Uncontrolled Hypertension","summary":"The purpose of this clinical trial is to measure the safety and efficacy of RTN-001 in adult participants with uncontrolled hypertension versus placebo.","conditions":["Uncontrolled Hypertension"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"RTN-001"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Matching placebo control"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Male or female patients age 18 to 75 years, inclusive, at the Screening Visit.\n* Uncontrolled HTN despite being on a stable regimen of 2-5 antihypertensive medications.\n* Mean BP of ≥135/80 mm Hg.\n* Body mass index of 18 to 35 kg/m2.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Mean seated SBP \\>175 mm Hg and/or DBP \\>110 mm Hg.\n* Current or planned use of nitrates and/or alpha-blockers or other drugs known to affect BP during the study period.\n* Participants who use PDE5 inhibitors for other indications that cannot or will not refrain from use of PDE5 inhibitors for 7 days before and during their entire period of participation in the study.\n* History of hypotension, fainting spells, blackouts or autonomic dysfunction, including orthostatic hypotension.\n* Known diagnosis of secondary hypertension (e.g. Cushing's Disease or hyperaldosteronism, renal fibrodysplasia, renal artery stenosis, etc., clinically significant aortic stenosis etc.).\n* Recent (within 3 months before the Screening Visit \\[Visit S1\\]) myocardial infarction; unstable angina leading to hospitalization; uncontrolled, symptomatic atrial fibrillation, or any cardiac arrhythmia that has not been clinically stable for at least 3 months prior to screening. Participants with implantable pacemakers or automatic implantable cardioverter defibrillators may be considered if deemed by the Investigator to be stable for the previous 3 months.\n* Uncontrolled hypothyroidism\n* Liver disease or dysfunction\n* Renal dysfunction (\\<45 mL/min/1.73m²) or glomerulonephritis\n* Active infection or major illness\n* Gastrointestinal conditions or procedures (including weight loss surgery \\[eg, Lap-Band or gastric bypass\\]) that may affect drug absorption.\n* Hematologic or coagulation disorders\n* Active malignancy\n* Unexplained creatine kinase (CK) \\>3 × ULN at any time before randomization\n* A known history of temporary or permanent partial or total vision loss\n* A known history of \"crowded\" optic disc.\n* A known history of retinitis pigmentosa, a rare genetic eye disease.\n* Any prescription or over-the counter drugs or herbal supplements known to be strong inhibitors of CYP3A4 enzymes\n* NHYA class III-IV symptoms of heart failure.\n* History of diabetes or suspected diabetes with glycosylated hemoglobin \\> 10% or fasting glucose \\>250 mg/dl at Screening Visit (S1).","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"75 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":280,"start":"2025-10-31","pcd":"2027-03","upd":"2026-11-04","sponsor":"Retension Pharmaceuticals. Inc.","areas":["other"],"central":["Clinical Information · 7036242024 · clinicalinformation@retensionpharmaceuticals.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Retension Clinical Site","city":"Alexander City","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35010","s":"R","lat":32.944,"lon":-85.9539,"c":"CRO Call Center · participate@worldwide.com"},{"f":"Retension Clinical Site","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35205","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"CRO Call Center"},{"f":"Retension Clinical Site","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35222","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"CRO Call Center · participate@worldwide.com"},{"f":"Retension Clinical Site","city":"Glendale","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85304","s":"R","lat":33.5386,"lon":-112.186,"c":"CRO Call Center · participate@worldwide.com"},{"f":"Ret